Report a missing session bus as a11y debugging, not as a warning.

When GTK finds no D-Bus session bus, it cannot reach the accessibility
bus and runs without one.  It said so with g_warning() on every start,
which on a system without D-Bus (zedBSD; the user decided GTK runs there
without portals or D-Bus) is a warning about the normal state.  The
message now goes to GTK's own a11y debugging (GTK_DEBUG=a11y shows it);
the behaviour is unchanged.

--- a/gtk/a11y/gtkatspicontext.c
+++ b/gtk/a11y/gtkatspicontext.c
@@ -1803,7 +1803,9 @@
 
   if (error != NULL)
     {
-      g_warning ("Unable to acquire session bus: %s", error->message);
+      /* A system without a session bus (zedBSD has no D-Bus) simply has no
+       * accessibility bus; say so only when a11y debugging is asked for. */
+      GTK_DEBUG (A11Y, "Unable to acquire session bus: %s", error->message);
       g_error_free (error);
       return NULL;
     }
